Concepts:
1. In binary form a number can be doubled by appending a 0 at the end of it.
2. 2k+1 is obtained by appending 1 in the binary representation of k
3. 2k is obtained by appending 0 in the binary representation of k
4. a xor b = c, in this expression a and c had the same parity(even or odd no. of 1 in binary)
5. x xor 1 = x with last bit changed 1001 xor 1 = 1000 10 xor 1 = 11

Builtin Function of GCC compiler

1. __builtin_popcount(n) : calculate the number of ones in binary representation of a given unsigned number
   __builtin_popcountl(n) : for long integer
   __builtin_popcountll(n) : for long long integer

odd parity: If a number contains odd no. of one in binary
even parity: if the number contains even no. of one in binary
2. __builtin_parity(n) : return true if number has odd parity in binary
return false if number has even parity in binary
   __builtin_parityl(n): for long integer
   __builtin_parityll(n): for long long integer

3. __builtin_clz: It count the number of leading zero before the first occurance of one
__builtin_clz(16) : 27
__builtin_clzll(16) : 59

4. __builtin_ctz: Count the number of trailing zeros, if any in binary
__builtin_ctz(16) : 4
__builtin_ctz(17) : 0
